{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"harpy","id":"651981368175230976","is_bot":0,"username":"harpsy_cored"},"author_id":"651981368175230976","channel_id":"865604031854411826","content":"The letter reads ||*Dear Mr. Finn Midask, I hope this letter finds you in good health. I feel as though I am at fault for my daughter's actions at the party, so I would like to personally apologize. My daughter is out of her depth with you. She does not realize the extent of which she is in love with you. I know the signs, as I was the same way when I met her father. Before she came to this city, she would spend hours every night, crying and talking about how lonely she was. When she met you, you were the only thing she talked about to me. She is afraid to lose you, because she does not want to end up alone again. I do not want my daughter to end up like her mother, cursed to be alone forever. Please, understand her fears. On another note, I would like you to teach her more about being in a relationship. She still has much to learn, and you need to be the one to teach her. Sincerely, Saria*||","created_at":"2021-07-23T17:34:23.075000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"868184282680672256","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
